# Copy to hooks/channel-ceiling.conf. Shared by two guards that watch the same shared
# files, so they only need configuring once:
#   - git-hooks/pre-commit's channel-file insertion ceiling: refuses a COMMIT that adds
#     more than LIMIT lines to one of these files in one go (a sign two sessions' entries
#     landed together).
#   - hooks/channel-size-guard.sh's growth band: warns once a file's TOTAL size crosses a
#     "sweep it soon" band, and refuses further growth once it crosses a hard stop —
#     checked live, on every Write/Edit/MultiEdit/Bash-append, not only at commit time.
#
# One optional LIMIT line (default 100, used only by pre-commit), then one line per file:
#   <repo-relative glob pattern>  [<unit> <band> <hard-stop>]
# The pattern is matched with a plain bash `case` glob — "NOTES.md" matches only a
# top-level file, "*/NOTES.md" matches one in any folder. <unit> is "words" or "lines".
# Leave the last three fields off a line to add a pattern to pre-commit's ceiling ONLY —
# channel-size-guard.sh ignores a line with no unit/band/stop. A pattern can appear on more
# than one line with a different unit (a file watched on both its word count and its line
# count). channel-size-guard.sh matches by the pattern's own BASENAME (it can't always see
# a file's full repo-relative path), so `*/NOTES.md` there just means "any NOTES.md".
#
# No file at all: neither guard does anything for any file — the safe default for a repo
# with no shared files several people or sessions append to.
LIMIT=100
NOTES.md          words 9000 15000
CHANGELOG.md
*/NOTES.md        words 9000 15000
